    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "> I'm not sure the end result in Sass will be any more readable than plain CSS, though :)\n\nFor me, no-brainer :)\n\n``` css\n/* REFINEMENT LIST */\n.ais-refinement-list {\n}\n.ais-refinement-list--header {\n  font-size: 1.2em;\n}\n.ais-refinement-list--body {\n}\n.ais-refinement-list--list {\n}\n.ais-refinement-list--item {\n}\n.ais-refinement-list--item__active {\n  font-weight: bold;\n}\n.ais-refinement-list--label {\n}\n.ais-refinement-list--checkbox {\n}\n.ais-refinement-list--count {\n  float: right;\n  display: inline-block;\n  background: black;\n  color: white;\n}\n.ais-refinement-list--footer {\n}\n```\n\nVS \n\n``` sass\n// REFINEMENT LIST\n+component(refinement-list)\n  +modifier(header)\n    font-size: 1.2em\n  +modifier(body)\n  +modifier(list)\n  +modifier(item)\n    +element(active)\n       font-weight: bold\n  +modifier(label)\n  +modifier(checkbox)\n  +modifier(count)\n    float: right\n    display: inline-block\n    background: black\n    color: white\n  +modifier(footer)\n```\n",
    "commit_id": "585d9a11365a68c3e904dd9e3ef13abaef0d825f",
    "created_at": "2015-10-22T10:46:55Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+@mixin component($component)\n+  .ais-#{$component}\n+    @content\n+\n+@mixin modifier($modifier)\n+  &--#{$modifier}\n+    @content\n+\n+@mixin element($element)\n+  &__#{$element}\n+    @content",
